Z||000006||ejayerik||12-21-2001||06:31 PM||||Looks like a script error. Try to upgrade with the 5.5 patch. If that doesn't work, try upgrading your IM. Sometimes they find the bug. If that doesn't work...upgrade to Explorer 6.0. If I knew the .dll file that was causing the problem I'd tell you to delete that and reinstall. It may be corrupt.<BR>Though the real problem is that you use AOL..lol<p>[This message has been edited by ejayerik (edited 12-21-2001).]||||reg||1
Z||000007||Cliff Pennock||12-21-2001||07:04 PM||||Could you try <A HREF="http://pip.pennock.nl/download/pip10x-107.zip" TARGET=_blank>this</A> version?<P>Just download it and unzip it in the PIP directory (usually \Program Files\Pip). You'll know if you installed this patch properly when at startup it says it's version 1.07.<P>This will not fix the problem, but it will give a little more information about the error. If you get the error, could you write down exactly what it says?<BR>||||reg||1
